    {
      "id": 6344941796681954,
      "plugin": "StochasticTelegraph",
      "model": "Fermata",
      "version": "2.0.17",
      "params": [],
      "rightModuleId": 4632602111214391,
      "data": {
        "text": "GYROBANK\n========\n\nThis is a set of six branching PHO oscillators, each with their own additive partial control. CV comes in and drives PHO 1 and 2 - then each of them drive two more PHOs. \n\nIt gets a little complicated here because PHO expects a simple ramp, from which it produces sines. Sending it a sine will result in a more complex waveform. \n\nWith a sample-and-hold setup you can create a lot of interesting patterns. Or crank it up to audio rate for loads of harmonically complex oscillations\n\nUse OFFSET on the incoming signal to play only a small portion of a 0-10v ramp over and over\n",
        "width": 3,
        "screen_colors": 1095216660480,
        "font_choice": "fonts/RobotoMono-Bold.ttf",
        "title_text": "GYROBANK"
      },
      "pos": [
        63,
        5
      ]
    },
